# Line-ending policy: LF everywhere, in the repository and in the working tree,
# on every platform. Without this file each contributor's core.autocrlf decides,
# and a Windows checkout rewrites every text file to CRLF on disk, which git
# then reports as a modification of every tracked file on any machine where
# that setting differs. All tracked files are already LF, so this changes no
# content; it only stops the working tree from drifting.

* text=auto eol=lf

# No binary files are tracked today. These rules exist so the first one added
# (a favicon, a screenshot) is not corrupted by the text handling above.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.svg  text eol=lf
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
